2026-10-13T16:33:08.4311656Z both empty), so the `admin` permission alone still opens these eight INSTANCE-GLOBAL
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4312663Z route groups to ANY admin-permissioned token, including one whose only membership is an
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4313392Z admin seat in a single workspace:
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4314543Z   1. POST|GET /v1/admin/self-update, POST /v1/admin/rollback, POST|GET /v1/admin/site-deploy
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4315424Z   2. GET /v1/plugins
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4316013Z   3. GET|PUT|DELETE /v1/plugins/settings/:plugin_name
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4317057Z   4. GET /v1/secrets, GET /v1/secrets/:name, GET /v1/secrets/:name/audit,
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4317807Z      PUT /v1/secrets/:name, DELETE /v1/secrets/:name
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4318430Z   5. POST /v1/status/incidents, POST /v1/status/incidents/:id/resolve
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4318886Z   6. POST /api/playground
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4319252Z   7. POST /api/workspaces/:workspace_slug/import
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4319720Z   8. GET /v1/instance/site-deploy, GET /v1/instance/metrics
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4320643Z On a SINGLE-TENANT instance that is fine — the only admin is the operator. On a
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4321553Z MULTI-TENANT one it hands your first customer-admin the instance: run-secrets in
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4322321Z cleartext, the instance-wide plugin credentials record, and the release itself.
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4323180Z Set BARKPARK_OPERATOR_EMAILS (comma-separated operator emails) and/or BARKPARK_OPERATOR_TOKEN_IDS
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4324495Z (comma-separated api_token ids) to arm the allowlist; once either is non-empty the
2026-10-13T16:33:08.4325417Z eight groups are allowlist-only and fail closed.
